How can banks integrate natural language processing into their day-to-day operations? 
Can you provide an example of a Java code that utilizes NLP for financial data analysis?
[Java code]
import java.util.Scanner;
import edu.stanford.nlp.simple.*;
public class FinancialAnalysis {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter transaction description: ");
        String description = sc.nextLine();
        System.out.println("Enter transaction amount: ");
        double amount = sc.nextDouble();
        // NLP analysis of transaction description
        Document doc = new Document(description);
        String[] tokens = doc.tokens().toArray(new String[0]);
        // Check for keywords related to fraud or suspicious activity
        for (String token : tokens) {
            if (token.equalsIgnoreCase("unauthorized") || token.equalsIgnoreCase("fraud")) {
                System.out.println("Suspicious activity detected. Please contact the bank immediately.");
                return;
            }
        }
        // Check for keywords related to overdraft or low balance
        for (String token : tokens) {
            if (token.equalsIgnoreCase("overdraft") || token.equalsIgnoreCase("low balance")) {
                System.out.println("Warning: Your account balance is low.");
                break;
            }
        }
        // Check for keywords related to deposits or withdrawals
        if (amount < 0) {
            System.out.println("Withdrawal of $" + (-1*amount) + " detected.");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Deposit of $" + amount + " detected.");
        }
    }
} 
Can you explain how this Java code can be used in financial institutions to analyze transaction data and identify potential fraud or suspicious activity?

