Here is the MATLAB code to unscramble the letters and output the correct names of the monuments:
```
% Load the XML file
xml_data = xmlread('monuments.xml');
% Get the list of monuments
monuments = xml_data.getElementsByTagName('monument');
% Loop through each monument and unscramble the letters
for i = 0:monuments.getLength-1
    % Get the scrambled letters and correct name of the monument
    monument = monuments.item(i);
    scrambled = char(monument.getElementsByTagName('scrambled').item(0).getFirstChild.getData);
    correct = char(monument.getElementsByTagName('correct').item(0).getFirstChild.getData);

    % Remove any spaces from the correct name
    correct = strrep(correct, ' ', '');

    % Sort the letters of the scrambled word
    sorted = sort(scrambled);

    % Find the indices of the sorted letters in the correct name
    indices = zeros(1, length(scrambled));
    for j = 1:length(scrambled)
        indices(j) = strfind(correct, sorted(j));
    end

    % Rearrange the letters of the correct name based on the indices
    unscrambled = '';
    for j = 1:length(indices)
        unscrambled = strcat(unscrambled, correct(indices == j));
    end

    % Display the unscrambled name
    disp(unscrambled);
end
```
This code uses the built-in `xmlread` function to load the XML file and `getElementsByTagName` to get the list of monuments. It then loops through each monument, gets the scrambled letters and correct name, removes any spaces from the correct name, sorts the letters of the scrambled word, finds the indices of the sorted letters in the correct name, rearranges the letters of the correct name based on the indices, and displays the unscrambled name.

